{"step_index":622,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T20:26:14Z","thinking":"**Evaluating History Page Functionality**\n\nThe history page requires a login check upon loading. If the user isn't logged in, or the token is invalid, the system needs to determine how to proceed. It should check for a stored token, offering a login option if none is found or displaying local history. Otherwise, it should fetch history data via API.\n\n\n**Handling Unauthorized Access Scenarios**\n\nThe system must handle 401 errors gracefully. A stale token requires removal from local storage. Display a session expiration message alongside a convenient one-click login to the customer account, followed by immediate history reload. If the API fetch fails or no token is found, local history should be used to prevent empty states.\n\n**Rendering History Table Data**\n\nPurchase entries are indicated with a green shopping cart badge and include a receipt link if a receipt ID is available via regex or `item.receiptId`. Verification entries display a blue shield badge, with statuses conditionally styled based on their verification status like \"DATABASE MATCH\" or \"NEEDS REVIEW\" or using a default of \"MATCH\". The action column includes a medicine view link for relevant entries.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\User\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\medcheck-bd\\\\client\\\\js\\\\main.js\"","EndLine":"520","StartLine":"470","toolAction":"\"Viewing main.js local history functions\"","toolSummary":"\"Check local history helper functions in main.js\""}}]}
