{"step_index":640,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T20:26:46Z","thinking":"**Improving History Page Behavior**\n\nThe history page's current behavior requires examination regarding user login status. When not logged in, the immediate redirect to login prevents viewing locally stored verification or purchase data. Consider prompting users to log in with a single-click or displaying the browser's local history instead. For logged-in users, `/api/history?type=${type}` fetches the required data.\n\n\n**Implementing Robust Error Handling**\n\nEncountering a 401 status requires clearing the authentication token and providing a quick demo login option. Displaying local history immediately after clearing the token prevents the table from appearing empty. Integrating server history with local history requires checking local storage during server history retrieval.\n\nThe receipt ID parsing logic must apply only to purchase items with associated notes. If the note matches a specific pattern, generate a receipt link. Finally, empty state displays for purchase and verification types require distinct, user-friendly messages with appropriate calls to action.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Upgraded history.html with seamless session recovery, local history fallback, clickable digital receipt buttons, and rich empty states for purchases and verifications.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n  <meta charset=\\\"UTF-8\\\">\\n  <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\\\">\\n  <title>Medicine History - MedCheck BD</title>\\n  <link href=\\\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css\\\" rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\">\\n  <link href=\\\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css\\\" rel=\\\"stylesheet\\\">\\n  